{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790714382,"nonce":"AE2At0LNY7QTLIt70yievT0pZX0=","title":"Author, save, and reopen sketch descriptions","message":"\u003c!-- ABOUTME: Defines the shared sketch-description authoring and persistence slice. --\u003e\n\u003c!-- ABOUTME: Covers description editing, desktop bundle saves, and browser-only transient authoring. --\u003e\n\n# Author, save, and reopen sketch descriptions\n\n## Parent\n\n02e51b7 / https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/84\n\n## What to build\n\nAdd a Description panel for the active sketch in the shared IDE. Provide editable metadata fields labelled exactly `title`, `order`, `enabled`, `categories`, and `tags`, alongside a Markdown body editor. Persist populated descriptions as example-schema-compatible frontmatter and Markdown on desktop Save and Save As; reopen the saved source and description together. Clearing the body removes only the description on the next save. Description-only edits participate in the existing dirty, discard, and private-recovery lifecycle. In the browser/PWA, provide authoring without sidecar persistence, gallery discovery, or misleading save claims. Keep bundled Examples immutable. Broken source remains saveable.\n\nUser stories: 1–13, 16, 26–27.\n\nRelated context only: broad requests 948a98c and 0ac47e5. This slice does not replace, close, or modify those issues.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The shared IDE provides a Description panel for the active sketch with editable fields labelled exactly `title`, `order`, `enabled`, `categories`, and `tags`, plus an editable Markdown body.\n- [ ] New descriptions default `order` to `0` and `enabled` to checked/true, and start with a nonempty `title` value subject to normal title validation. Metadata is held separately from Markdown: `title` is a nonempty string, `order` is finite numeric, `enabled` is boolean, and `categories` and `tags` are string lists. Blank or whitespace-only Markdown is treated as no description, and metadata alone does not create one. Do not add title requirements beyond the schema.\n- [ ] Panel moves and workspace layout changes retain the active description edits. Switching to a new sketch, opening a file, selecting an example, or otherwise replacing the active document uses the existing unsaved-change protection for description-only edits as well as source edits.\n- [ ] Private recovery includes description and metadata edits and restores them with the active document, without writing source or description files in the background.\n- [ ] On explicit desktop Save, populated description data is written with YAML frontmatter validated against the same metadata schema as bundled examples, plus Markdown in the active sketch bundle. Punctuation, Unicode, multiline Markdown, and category/tag string lists round-trip correctly; do not treat user metadata or Markdown as trusted bundled HTML.\n- [ ] Preserve once-only format-on-save behavior; capturing a thumbnail does not trigger another language execution.\n- [ ] Desktop Save As carries the current description and metadata into the copy, preserves the original sketch, and retains existing tutor-session copy behavior.\n- [ ] Reopening a saved desktop sketch loads its source and description together. Opening a sketch with no description starts with an empty panel and never leaks the previous sketch's description.\n- [ ] Saving after clearing the Markdown body removes only that sketch's `description.md`; its source, thumbnail, sessions, unrelated user files, and folder remain intact.\n- [ ] Broken or invalid GIC source remains saveable; language or preview failure does not prevent saving source and a populated description. These language/preview failures are distinct from native I/O failures.\n- [ ] In the browser/PWA, the Description panel supports transient authoring. Source download neither claims to persist the description nor resets/discards it, and no description or thumbnail sidecar or native Sketches gallery is provided.\n- [ ] Bundled Examples remain immutable; saving a personal sketch cannot modify shipped example content.\n- [ ] Automated shared Playwright tests drive the real editor and cover exact labels/defaults, description-only dirty/discard behavior, document switching without metadata leakage, and unchanged source-file open/download behavior. Do not use hidden DOM state or a test-only bridge.\n- [ ] Automated desktop integration tests use real temporary files and cover description save, round-trip, deletion, Save As, language-error/broken-source saving, and preservation of unrelated files; do not mock file operations.\n- [ ] Native I/O failures surface an error; cancellation is a normal outcome and does not report an error. In both cases dirty edits remain dirty, no false save success is reported, the original bundle remains usable, and unrelated files remain untouched.\n- [ ] Packaged macOS acceptance exercises the real editor and native save/open workflow: edit every field and Markdown, save, inspect and reopen the bundle, verify edits survive restart, exercise Save As and clearing, and confirm Examples remain unchanged. Native I/O failures surface errors; cancellation does not. Both preserve dirty edits, avoid false save success, and leave the original bundle usable.\n\n## Blocked by\n\nNone.","files":null}]}